nodecode-mask is a rewrite of PerryLink's PerryLink/dsh-mask:

  https://github.com/PerryLink/dsh-mask
  commit 11402b9b71cda30233934b8f77aaca776dbe185d
  Apache-2.0 (LICENSE, which carries the stock "Copyright [yyyy] [name of
  copyright owner]" placeholder; package.json names the author PerryLink)

LICENSE is that repository's LICENSE file, unchanged.

What was rewritten: the whole plugin, in Common Lisp, on the Nodecode cell
contract. The ten regular expressions, their confidences, the overlap rule
that keeps the earliest span and the more confident one at the same start, the
numbered `<TYPE_N>` placeholders that give the same words the same number, and
the `/mask` and `mask_test` surface are the original's, ported one for one.

What was left out, and why: the plugin hooked dsh's inbound agent step and,
with its `tools` scope, its tool-result step — Nodecode has one seam for the
outgoing request, the wire fold, so only user text is masked and tool results
pass whole. The restore table was a per-session store on disk, and `/mask
restore` hashed the session id into a file name; here the placeholders live in
the image for the length of a run and the restore file is named for the
session the command runs in. The person and address detectors, which the
original declared but could only fill from an external recognizer, are not
offered. What a restore writes is one file per session, mode 0600 where the
implementation can say so.
